1. **C — missing degree/invariant compatibility.**

   Quotes:

   > `inheritedE : ℕ`  
   > `inheritedF : ℕ`

   and

   > \(|S_{\lambda,r'}|=De'\deg r'\)

   while

   > \(e=e_{\mathcal C}e'\), \(f=f_{\mathcal C}\deg r'\).

   The carrier never requires
   \[
   D=e_{\mathcal C}f_{\mathcal C}.
   \]
   Consequently local \(e,f\)-forcing yields orbit degree
   \[
   e_{\mathcal C}f_{\mathcal C}e'\deg r',
   \]
   not the claimed \(De'\deg r'\). The proof’s lower-bound sum therefore need not equal the side-accounting total. This makes HE7.A false for the stated abstract interface, even though the five intended candidates appear numerically compatible.

2. **G — “consumed sides” do not cover the theorem’s quantifier.**

   R1 supplies accounting only

   > “for every consumed side \(\lambda\)”

   but HE7.A concludes

   > “every side of \(P\) has slope strictly greater than \(T\)”.

   No field identifies the certificate’s finite side set with all sides of the lower hull \(P\). The replacement proof therefore does not establish clause 1 as stated.

3. **G — key-boundary data is attached at the wrong type level.**

   R1 simultaneously requires in `SigmaBlock`

