   and adds

   > `keyBoundary : Option (KeyBoundaryCertificate C poly)`.

   A non-key-free polynomial cannot inhabit `SigmaBlock`, so the optional certificate there cannot preprocess that polynomial. The promised “key-boundary certificate when the input is not key-free” has no displayed typed entry point outside `SigmaBlock`; `KeyBoundaryResult` is described but not actually signed.

4. **G — the HE6 empty transition relation cannot support the master’s repeated branches.**

   Quote:

   > “For HE6, a one-shot record may use the empty transition relation”

   Yet `SigmaStepData` must expose linear-refine and child-jump transitions, and HE7.A clauses 3 and 5 require continuation whenever a repeated residual factor occurs. No HE6-side hypothesis says all consumed residuals are separable or terminal. Thus the proposed empty relation cannot instantiate the full master record.

5. **G — the Lean sketch conflates valued points with residue targets.**

